        "India's anti-dumping regime is designed to protect domestic producers of the investigated products from unfairly priced imports, and the legal test focuses on the injury to those producers. Our results show that the duties also impose substantial costs on downstream users, which are not part of the injury determination. The costs are concentrated in sectors — chemicals-based manufacturing, plastics processing, pharmaceuticals — that are among India's most export-oriented and that the government has sought to promote through other policies. A one-standard-deviation increase in exposure reduces exports by 4.7 percent, an effect that undercuts the objective of raising India's share of global manufacturing exports.",
