        "Concordance. Harmonised System six-digit codes in the Global Antidumping Database are mapped to the 130 sectors of the 2007–08 input–output table using the concordance between the Indian Trade Classification and the National Industrial Classification published by the Ministry of Commerce, supplemented by manual matching for 46 codes. Within each input–output sector, we allocate the input coefficient across Harmonised System products in proportion to their shares in Indian imports in 1996–1998, before our sample period.",
